<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Debug build type only (src/debug/, never merged into release). Without
  this, VyaparApiFactory's own loopback carve-out is dead on-device: its
  KDoc admits as much ("On-device the manifest's usesCleartextTraffic=false
  backstops this check") — a blanket usesCleartextTraffic="false" with no
  domain-config has no automatic loopback exception, it blocks cleartext to
  127.0.0.1 exactly as it blocks cleartext to anywhere else. The carve-out
  in VyaparApiFactory.create() only ever did real work for JVM unit tests
  (MockWebServer, no Android OS enforcement at all) until this file existed.

  base-config stays false, matching :core:network's manifest and docs/14's
  "TLS everywhere" — only these specific hosts get the exception, so this
  can't accidentally be pointed at a real non-TLS host during a demo.

  The signaling WebSocket (OkHttpSignalingClient, CallController.openTransport)
  is a SEPARATE connection from the REST base URL: it dials whatever
  signaling_url the session-create response carries — SIGNALING_PUBLIC_URL
  in backend/.env, the host's real LAN IP, not 127.0.0.1 — because that
  value has to be reachable directly from the phone's real WiFi radio, not
  through the adb-reverse USB tunnel (TCP-only, and only forwards the two
  ports named in the manifest's own comment). Found live: session-create
  succeeded fine over the loopback carve-out above, then the WS connect
  failed with UnknownServiceException("CLEARTEXT communication to
  <LAN IP> not permitted") because that host was never added here.

  REPLACE 192.168.1.11 with `ipconfig`'s current Wi-Fi IPv4 address if it
  changes (new network, DHCP lease renewal) — must match COTURN_HOST /
  SIGNALING_PUBLIC_URL in backend/.env exactly, same as the manifest's
  BASE_URL comment already asks for the REST side.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">localhost</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">192.168.1.11</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
